(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[7 1 "// PEP 734's interpreters (queue 230; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 230\"): several Interps in one process over"] [8 1 "// the one GIL, CPython 3.14.10's Python/crossinterp.c, Python/crossinterp_data_lookup.h, Python/crossinterp_exceptions.h"] [9 1 "// and Modules/_interpretersmodule.c ported. An interpreter's state is its *Interp, reached through current.Interp as"] [10 1 "// before; nothing here runs in a program that creates no interpreter, but the comparison in gil.take (interpSwitch) and"] [11 1 "// finTrack's owner. A session (_PyXI_Enter, _PyXI_Exit) runs on the calling goroutine under a new *Thread of the target"] [12 1 "// interpreter: one OS thread, two thread states, as CPython's."] [23 1 "// interpConfig is PyInterpreterConfig. gil: \"default\", \"shared\" or \"own\": pyi has the one GIL (the design's table), the"] [24 1 "// value is data."] [30 1 "// xiState is an Interp's state for interpreters: what CPython keeps in PyInterpreterState beyond the module table."] [38 32 "// __main__.__loader__ set (the first session)"] [39 32 "// threads started and not finished (_thread._count)"] [40 32 "// the heap types' getters (_PyXIData_RegisterClass)"] [41 32 "// sync_module's per-interpreter cache, by __main__'s file"] [43 27 "// _interpqueues' module state"] [44 27 "// _interpchannels' module state"] [45 2 "// overrideMultiInterp is _imp._override_multi_interp_extensions_check's override (-1 never, 1 always, 0 the config)"] [49 1 "// interpRegs are the active interpreter's registers (the design's table): package variables the hot paths read, an"] [50 1 "// interpreter's own, swapped by interpSwitch."] [56 2 "// the module states a native module keeps in package variables: _asyncio's, _csv's, os.register_at_fork's"] [60 2 "// maxStrDigits: sys.set_int_max_str_digits' limit, each interpreter's own (interp->long_state; py-eval-1122)"] [67 25 "// the live interpreters, oldest first"] [69 2 "// xiEndHooks run when an interpreter ends (the queues' and the channels' items unbound)"] [73 1 "// interpSwitch makes in's registers the active ones."] [89 1 "// switchThread makes t the running thread on this goroutine (PyThreadState_Swap)."] [102 41 "// the main interpreter has its own GIL, as CPython's reports it"] [105 1 "// namedConfig is init_named_config."] [109 94 "// _PyInterpreterConfig_INIT"] [131 1 "// update is _PyInterpreterConfig_UpdateFromDict (all: _InitFromDict, every field required)."] [203 1 "// newSubInterp is Py_NewInterpreterFromConfig: init_interp_settings' checks, then a fresh Interp: its sys, importlib and"] [204 1 "// the rest fill in at its first import, its __main__ exists at once."] [215 2 "// the limit the configuration gives (-X int_max_str_digits, PYTHONINTMAXSTRDIGITS, else 4300), not the main interpreter's"] [216 2 "// current one (py-eval-1122: test_int's test_int_max_str_digits_is_per_interpreter)"] [224 32 "// a new __main__'s, as pylifecycle.c's add_main_module leaves it"] [231 1 "// end is Py_EndInterpreter: the non-daemon threads joined, atexit's functions run, the streams flushed; the interpreter"] [232 1 "// leaves the table and its items in the queues and channels are unbound."] [268 1 "// The moment of an interpreter handle's death (queue 553; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 553\"): a stdlib"] [269 1 "// interpreter (_interpreters.create(reqrefs=True)) ends when its last handle's __del__ drops its references (decref), and"] [270 1 "// its items in the queues and channels are unbound then, as reference counting does at `del interp`. pyi's moment at del"] [271 1 "// (finDeleted, queue 222) asks Go's collector within a budget of a tenth of the wall time; past it, while a subinterpreter"] [272 1 "// is held by handles, the deletion is owed (xiDeathOwed) and settled by one collection round before the next operation"] [273 1 "// whose answer depends on interpreters being alive: the queues' get, get_count, is_full and list_all, the channels'"] [274 1 "// recv, get_count, get_info, list_all and list_interpreters."] [277 1 "// xiHeldByHandles is whether a subinterpreter is alive with handles' references (refs > 0 under reqrefs)."] [287 1 "// xiSettleDeaths is the owed collection round (xiDeathOwed), at most once per owed deletion."] [305 1 "// isRunningMain is is_running_main: a thread runs __main__."] [308 1 "// the static exceptions (crossinterp_exceptions.h), made on first use: shared as CPython's static types are; pyi's"] [309 1 "// NotShareableError is shared too (CPython's heap type per interpreter), so `except` matches across a session"] [348 1 "// notShareable is set_notshareableerror with a cause."] [358 1 "// xiLookupFailure is _set_xid_lookup_failure."] [373 1 "// xiUnwrap is _PyXI_UnwrapNotShareableError: a NotShareableError's cause raised in its place."] [381 1 "// xiData is _PyXIData_t: the owner's id, new_object as a closure over a copy of the data, the release of what it binds."] [397 1 "// xiGetter is _PyXIData_getdata_t."] [402 1 "// xiLookup is lookup_getdata by the object's exact type."] [479 1 "// xiBufferViewType is _interpreters' XIBufferView: what a shared memoryview's obj shows."] [496 16 "// queue 249: the other interpreter's view holds no export of its own"] [501 1 "// xiGetBasic is _get_xidata."] [515 1 "// xiGetData is _PyObject_GetXIData; fallback: _PyXIDATA_FULL_FALLBACK."] [540 1 "// xiMainFile is _Py_GetMainfile: __main__.__file__, \"\" when none."] [550 1 "// xiPickleData is _PyPickle_GetXIData."] [571 1 "// xiMissingMainAttr is check_missing___main___attr."] [581 1 "// xiPickleLoads is _PyPickle_Loads: on a missing __main__ attribute, once more with a __main__ loaded from the original"] [582 1 "// file under a bogus name, cached per interpreter (ensure_isolated_main)."] [627 1 "// xiGlobalNames counts co's LOAD_GLOBALs (identify_unbound_names): in globals, in builtins, neither."] [646 1 "// xiVerifyStateless is _PyCode_VerifyStateless."] [661 1 "// xiVerifyFunction is _PyFunction_VerifyStateless."] [675 1 "// xiReturnsOnlyNone is _PyCode_ReturnsOnlyNone: no generator, each return's value the constant None."] [695 1 "// xiFunctionData is _PyFunction_GetXIData: only stateless functions; the code shared (marshal's copy would equal it),"] [696 1 "// a new function over the running __main__'s globals on the other side."] [720 1 "// xiScript is get_script_xidata (pure 0): the code of a function, a code object or a compiled text."] [763 1 "// xiExcInfo is _PyXI_excinfo."] [787 2 "// a traceback.TracebackException, formatted"] [816 1 "// format is _PyXI_excinfo_format, \"\" and false for None."] [838 1 "// asObject is _PyXI_excinfo_AsObject."] [866 1 "// apply is _PyXI_excinfo_Apply: exc of t with the snapshot's text."] [875 1 "// xiSession is _PyXI_session."] [882 1 "// xiEnter is _enter_session and _PyInterpreterState_SetRunningMain."] [897 3 "// init_importlib's part a new __main__ shows: its __loader__ is BuiltinImporter"] [910 1 "// exit is _exit_session."] [947 1 "// xiSharedNS is _create_sharedns and _fill_sharedns (no fallback)."] [957 3 "// _copy_string_obj_raw: the name as UTF-8 (PyUnicode_AsUTF8AndSize: a lone surrogate's UnicodeEncodeError)"] [977 1 "// xiCall is struct interp_call; xiRun is _run_in_interpreter."] [1007 3 "// a dict goes by pickle (no getter for it)"] [1022 1 "// wrapNotShareable is wrap_notshareable."] [1030 1 "// xiFailure is the override of a session's error: 0 uncaught, else its _PyXI_errcode's meaning."] [1038 1 "// xiApplyNotShareable is _PyXI_ApplyError's _PyXI_ERR_NOT_SHAREABLE."] [1047 1 "// xiRun runs a script (code) or a call in in, the updates applied to __main__ first: the result, the excinfo of an"] [1048 1 "// uncaught exception, or err raised directly."] [1114 2 "// the preserved result: a copy when the session switched interpreters"] [1166 1 "// xiProtect runs f with a Go panic as a SystemError, so that the session always exits."] [1198 1 "// interpID is _PyInterpreterState_ObjectToID."] [1233 1 "// resolveInterp is resolve_interp (every pyi interpreter is ready once made)."] [1602 1 "// ExtSubinterp is a legacy subinterpreter made through the C API (py-eval-1122: pyctypes' Py_NewInterpreter, for"] [1603 1 "// _testcapi's run_in_subinterp): the interpreter and the session the calling thread entered it with."] [1609 1 "// ExtNewInterpreter is Py_NewInterpreter: a legacy subinterpreter (whenceLegacyCAPI, the \"legacy\" config), entered by the"] [1610 1 "// calling thread, whose thread state is the new interpreter's until ExtEndInterpreter."] [1628 1 "// ExtEndInterpreter is Py_EndInterpreter: the session left (the thread back in the interpreter it came from), then the"] [1629 1 "// interpreter ended (its threads joined, its atexit functions run)."] [1635 1 "// ExtSubinterpExtensionAllowed is Python/import.c's _PyImport_CheckSubinterpIncompatibleExtensionAllowed for the C"] [1636 1 "// world's extension modules (arbace/pyctypes; queue 594): in a subinterpreter that checks (its"] [1637 1 "// check_multi_interp_extensions, or _imp._override_multi_interp_extensions_check's override) a module that does not"] [1638 1 "// support subinterpreters is an ImportError."] [1650 1 "// ExtInSubinterp is whether the active interpreter is a subinterpreter, and whether its config asks for its own GIL"] [1651 1 "// (interp->ceval.own_gil)."] [1660 1 "// overrideMultiInterpCheck is _imp._override_multi_interp_extensions_check(override): the old value."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[78 22] [134 53] [155 28] [170 20] [184 22] [185 42] [218 36] [337 27] [375 20] [405 39] [434 58] [521 27] [522 31] [526 28] [542 65] [543 47] [608 25] [609 62] [698 31] [706 55] [734 24] [750 43] [779 49] [780 23] [784 23] [855 24] [899 52] [900 55] [901 31] [918 26] [936 53] [958 43] [991 28] [997 34] [1001 27] [1002 41] [1006 28] [1008 45] [1051 28] [1053 32] [1094 44] [1100 47] [1118 38] [1130 24] [1169 20] [1177 20] [1178 23] [1188 28] [1202 27] [1227 27] [1240 34] [1247 33] [1289 44] [1303 33] [1355 78] [1418 30] [1427 27] [1447 24] [1465 30] [1470 29] [1552 30] [1583 45] [1588 40] [1644 36]]} (go/file "interpreters.go" :imports [


